<gpx version="1.1" creator="Flores Race Planner (pipeline/export_gpx.py)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <name>S06 Ebulobo and the Nagekeo plains</name>
    <desc>Section 06 of the Flores Race traverse: Back over the plateau, down to the rice plains. 141.1 km, +3342 m / -3320 m, starts at km 657 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:57Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.843000" lon="120.857000">
    <ele>14.4</ele>
    <name>Aimere</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: port | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- South-coast port of Ngada Regency, ~1 hour south of Bajawa; ASDP ferry to Waingapu (Sumba, Tue/Fri) and Kupang. Exact pier coordinates not found in sources; placed at a low-elevation coastal point inside Ngada near the d</desc>
    <sym>Anchor</sym>
    <type>anchor/port</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.824000" lon="121.052000">
    <ele>1087.2</ele>
    <name>Mataloko</name>
    <desc>km 47.0 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: reliable | sleep: guesthouse -- Golewa district capital on the Trans-Flores highway ~17 km ESE of Bajawa; St. Yohanes Berchmans minor seminary (European-style, colonial era) and the Mataloko geothermal field (20+ hot springs). Kemah Tabor retreat house</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.766700" lon="121.164400">
    <ele>500.7</ele>
    <name>Boawae</name>
    <desc>km 78.7 | kind: town | resupply: basic | water: reliable | sleep: homestay -- Main south-central town of Nagekeo Regency, on the northwest slope of Ebulobo volcano, on the Trans-Flores highway. Position corrected ~13.0 km to the Kantor Camat Boawae / Polsek Boawae cluster (Overture Maps place them</desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.575600" lon="121.280700">
    <ele>36.4</ele>
    <name>Mbay</name>
    <desc>km 141.1 | kind: town | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Administrative capital of Nagekeo Regency, on the Aesesa coastal plain (the largest rice-growing lowland on Flores), north coast. Desk position corrected ~17.3 km from an earlier unverified placement to the Civic Center </desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.830000" lon="120.851000">
    <ele>46.0</ele>
    <name>Aimere Arak Coast</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] The south-coast strip around Aimere port, known for small-scale distilling of arak (palm/lontar spirit) alongside its role as the Ngada ferry port to Sumba and Kupang.</desc>
    <sym>Waypoint</sym>
    <type>poi/other</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.794480" lon="120.970883">
    <ele>1184.0</ele>
    <name>Bajawa</name>
    <desc>[resupply] Cool highland capital of Ngada Regency (~1,100-1,300 m); market town and the region's main resupply point between the north coast and the Ngada villages.</desc>
    <sym>Waypoint</sym>
    <type>poi/other</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.877400" lon="120.985700">
    <ele>831.0</ele>
    <name>Bena</name>
    <desc>[anchor] A Ngada megalithic village of nine clans at the foot of Inerie, with paired ngadhu (male) and bhaga (female) ancestor shrines around a stone-terraced central square; among the more visited traditional villages in Ngada.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.896000" lon="120.991000">
    <ele>394.5</ele>
    <name>Gurusina</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] Ngada megalithic village commonly cited ~21 km from Bajawa; a fire on 13 August 2018 burned 27 of 33 traditional houses and 6 sacred structures, since rebuilt with traditional materials and techniques.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.878000" lon="120.953000">
    <ele>2129.2</ele>
    <name>Inerie</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike] A near-perfect stratovolcano cone (2,245 m) south of Bajawa overlooking the Savu Sea; the highest peak in Ngada and the visual anchor of the megalithic-village section. Not currently active.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.869500" lon="120.986000">
    <ele>934.2</ele>
    <name>Luba</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] A small Ngada megalithic village a few hundred metres from Bena, four clans, ngadhu and bhaga shrines decorated with carved horses, buffalo and snakes; quieter and less visited than its famous neighbour.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.833000" lon="121.061000">
    <ele>1062.3</ele>
    <name>Mataloko Hot Springs</name>
    <desc>[highlight] A geothermal field in the Todabelu/Mataloko cluster (PLTP Mataloko geothermal plant, Seminari Todabelu) with more than 20 hot springs up to 95 degC, spread across ~1,000 ha in Todabelu village, Golewa district.</desc>
    <sym>Swimming Area</sym>
    <type>poi/hot-spring</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.708500" lon="121.086900">
    <ele>318.8</ele>
    <name>Mengeruda Hot Spring</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Hot spring pools fed by a warm river in Piga village, Soa sub-district, ~23.5 km north of Bajawa, close to Soa airport; a natural stopover on the climb from Riung to the Bajawa plateau.</desc>
    <sym>Swimming Area</sym>
    <type>poi/hot-spring</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.708612" lon="121.057901">
    <ele>431.7</ele>
    <name>Turelelo-Soa Airport</name>
    <desc>[resupply] The airfield serving Bajawa (IATA BJW), in Soa sub-district ~23.5 km north of Bajawa town; scheduled flights to Kupang and Ende.</desc>
    <sym>Airport</sym>
    <type>poi/airport</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.840700" lon="120.961200">
    <ele>1113.0</ele>
    <name>Tololela</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position unverified] A Ngada megalithic village in Manubhara, Jerebuu district, ~30 km from Bajawa on a steep hillside (~650 m); fewer tour groups reach it than Bena.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.833000" lon="121.053000">
    <ele>1096.7</ele>
    <name>Wogo</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Old Ngada megalithic village near Mataloko, ~30 minutes east of Bajawa; the resettled 'new' Wogo sits by the road, the megalith complex of 'old' Wogo is ~1.5 km further on foot.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.835000" lon="120.980500">
    <ele>1537.4</ele>
    <name>Wolobobo Hill</name>
    <desc>[highlight] A sunrise viewpoint hill (~1,700 m) in Turekisa village, ~15 km from Bajawa, with a panoramic view of Inerie volcano and the Bajawa plateau.</desc>
    <sym>Scenic Area</sym>
    <type>poi/viewpoint</type>
  </wpt>
